 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 550654,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Suppose that a neural network has been trained to classify students as likely to graduate or not likely to graduate based on various input parameters. There is a single output neuron having four inputs, <span data-math=\"x_1,x_2,x_3,\"></span> and one output, <span data-math=\"y\"></span>. The output <span data-math=\"y\"></span> is used to make the classification. The weights of the three inputs of this neuron are <span data-math=\"w_1=0.25\"></span>, <span data-math=\"w_2=0.09\"></span>, and <span data-math=\"w_3=-0.31\"></span>. The bias of the neuron is <span data-math=\"b=-0.23\"></span>. Find the output <span data-math=\"y\"></span> if <span data-math=\"{(x_1,x_2,x_3)}=(0.4,-1.2,0.6)\"></span> and if the activation function is:\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: lower-roman;\">\n<li>ReLU</li>\n<li>Leaky ReLU defined by max⁡ (0.2x,x)</li>\n<li>Sigmoid</li>\n<li>Softplus</li>\n</ol>\n\n",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<br><ol style=\"list-style-type: lower-roman;\">\n<li><span data-math=\"0\"></span></li>\n<li><span data-math=\"-0.0848\"></span></li>\n<li><span data-math=\"0.396\"></span></li>\n<li><span data-math=\"0.503\"></span></li>\n</ol>\n\n\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"w\\cdot x+b=w_1x_1+w_2x_2+w_3x_3+b=0.25{(0.4)}+0.09{(-1.2)}+{(-0.31})(0.6)-0.23=-0.424\"></span><br>\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: lower-roman;\"><br>\n<li><span data-math=\"\\text{ReLU}{(-0.424)}=0\"></span>, since <span data-math=\"-0.424<0\"></span></li>\n<li><span data-math=\"\\text{LReLU}{(-0.424)}=\\text{max}{(0.2{(-0.424)},-0.424)}=\\text{max}{(-0.0848,-0.424)}=-0.0848\"></span></li>\n<li><span data-math=\"\\sigma{(-0.424)}=\\frac1{1+e^{-(-0.424)}}=0.396\"></span></li>\n<li>Softplus <span data-math=\"{(-0.424)}=\\text{ln}{(1+e^{-0.424})}=0.503\"></span></li>\n</ol>\n"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 550655,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Which of the four activation functions, applied at the output layer, would be best suited for this classification task? Using this activation function, how would the neural network classify the student?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "See Solution Manual"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "Because we are seeking a probability (how likely it is for a student to graduate), the best choice is sigmoid, as the outputs must lie between 0 and 1, which can be interpreted as a probability score. Since we obtained <span data-math=\"y=0.396\"></span>, we would classify the student as only 39.6% likely to graduate (or not likely to graduate)."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
